July 26, 2026\n    35→- **Category:** Full AI IDE\n    36→\n    37→### [EasyUseAIDE](https://github.com/john-ops-lab/EasyUseAIDE)\n    38→面向个人开发者的跨 IDE Agent AI 编码工程化规则、Skills 与项目交付模板。Cross-IDE Agent AI coding engineering rules, Skills & project delivery templates for individual developers.\n    39→- **Launch Date:** July 23, 2026\n    40→- **Category:** Full AI IDE/Cross-Platform\n    41→\n    42→---\n    43→\n    44→## 2. AI Coding CLIs or Terminal Agents\n    45→\n    46→### [bbarit-agent-oss](https://github.com/bbarit/bbarit-agent-oss)\n    47→Open-source AI coding agent for your terminal — one Rust binary, 15+ LLM providers, 1,000+ models. A self-hostable Claude Code / Codex CLI alternative (MIT).\n    48→- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n    49→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI\n    50→\n    51→### [pi-dispatch](https://github.com/edgehero/pi-dispatch)\n    52→Run the pi coding agent as a service — triggered on demand, on a cron schedule, or by a GitHub issue or pull request — in a container you control, with a durable queue, a spend cap, and a live admin panel.\n    53→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n    54→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Service\n    55→\n    56→### [infinitty](https://github.com/jasonkneen/infinitty)\n    57→Native insanely fast terminal built for agents.\n    58→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n    59→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Terminal\n    60→\n    61→### [plank](https://github.com/aovestdipaperino/plank)\n    62→Interactive terminal coding agent in Rust — runs the DeepSeek V4 Flash model locally on macOS (Metal), with a Ratatui TUI, a full tool suite, MCP, and persistent sessions.\n    63→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n    64→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI\n    65→\n    66→### [logan-cli](https://github.com/hoodini/logan-cli)\n    67→Logan CLI - terminal AI coding agent by Yuval Avidani (YUV.AI). Fork of xAI Grok Build.\n    68→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n    69→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI\n    70→\n    71→### [GrokDesk](https://github.com/KAMIENDER/GrokDesk)\n    72→Grok Build, beyond the terminal — native macOS workspace with full agent visibility, shared CLI sessions, and quota-aware multi-account routing.\n    73→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n    74→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/macOS Native\n    75→\n    76→### [Agent Manager](https://github.com/YoanWai/agent-manager)\n    77→Terminal UI to manage AI coding-agent sessions (Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Grok Build) in tmux: live status, group tree, live pane preview, resource gauges.\n    78→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n    79→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Session Manager\n    80→\n    81→### [agent-console](https://github.com/buhuipao/agent-console)\n    82→A local terminal control plane for Codex and Claude Code sessions—discover, monitor, resume, and work beside persistent workspace shells.\n    83→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n    84→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Control Plane\n    85→\n    86→### [Citizen-Agent](https://github.com/ElarineNycanis/Citizen-Agent)\n    87→多模型开源 AI 终端助手，支持模型自由切换，集成视觉理解、AI 生图、音乐播放与 5 路并行子代理。An open-source AI terminal assistant with dynamic model switching, built-in vision understanding, AI image generation, music playback, and 5 parallel sub-agents.\n    88→- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n    89→- **Category:** AI Coding CLI/Multi-Model\n    90→\n    91→---\n    92→\n    93→## 3. Workflow-Specific AI Tools (debugging, refactoring, test generation)\n    94→\n    95→### [Kritt](https://github.com/Kritt-ai/open-kritt)\n    96→Orchestrate AI agents to find real vulnerabilities in code.\n    97→- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n    98→- **Category:** Security/Code Analysis\n    99→\n   100→### [ponytail](https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved)\n   101→Makes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev in the room. The best code is the code you never wrote.\n   102→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   103→- **Category:** Refactoring/Code Optimization\n   104→\n   105→### [code-humanizer](https://github.com/LeonardNJU/code-humanizer)\n   106→humanizer, but for code — an agent skill that removes AI-generated code slop: duplicated helpers, try-import fallbacks, broad excepts, speculative abstractions. Test-gated, behavior-preserving.\n   107→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n   108→- **Category:** Refactoring/Code Cleanup\n   109→\n   110→### [idea-refiner-skill](https://github.com/BURIBURI-ZAEMON1/idea-refiner-skill)\n   111→Refine an early idea or creative concept into a coherent, evidence-aware design and durable Markdown master spec/PRD.\n   112→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   113→- **Category:** Product Design/Planning\n   114→\n   115→### [idea-starter](https://github.com/ky-zo/idea-starter)\n   116→Batteries-included, agent-guided starter for turning an idea into a deployed product.\n   117→- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n   118→- **Category:** Product Development Workflow\n   119→\n   120→### [idea-clarifier](https://github.com/guage1029/idea-clarifier)\n   121→一个在写 PRD 前无情拷问产品想法、澄清需求价值与商业假设的 Agent Skill。An Agent Skill that ruthlessly questions product ideas before writing PRDs, clarifying demand value and business assumptions.\n   122→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n   123→- **Category:** Product Requirements\n   124→\n   125→### [Instruckt Laravel](https://github.com/sam-jamestty1474/instruckt-laravel-mcp-debug-tool)\n   126→Instruckt Laravel v2026 is a Laravel/PHP package for live visual debugging of AI development flows, combining observability, MCP tooling, and AI-friendly feedback.\n   127→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   128→- **Category:** Debugging/Observability\n   129→\n   130→### [Multi-LLM Debugging Bridge](https://github.com/HoziMurayama/Multi-LLM-Debugging-Bridge)\n   131→An MCP server that connects multiple OpenAI-compatible LLMs with shared tool access. Inspired by rubber duck debugging, it lets users discuss problems with different AI models, gather diverse insights, perform research, and compare responses.\n   132→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   133→- **Category:** Debugging/Multi-Model\n   134→\n   135→### [vibe-coding-toolkit](https://github.com/derek030208-design/vibe-coding-toolkit)\n   136→Curated Claude Code skills for AI code quality control & creative writing.\n   137→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n   138→- **Category:** Code Quality/Workflow\n   139→\n   140→---\n   141→\n   142→## 4. AI Code Agents with Project/Workspace Memory\n   143→\n   144→### [MemTensor](https://github.com/MemTensor/memmy-agent)\n   145→A personal AI agent & local memory hub for all AI agents like Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw and Hermes Agent. Gives every AI one shared, fully controlled memory and persistent context — all AI remember the same you.\n   146→- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n   147→- **Category:** Memory/Persistent Context\n   148→\n   149→### [cindy](https://github.com/makecindy/cindy)\n   150→Consider it done. The open-source AI agent that works out of the box. 想到，就能做到。开源、开箱即用的 AI Agent。\n   151→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   152→- **Category:** General Purpose Agent/Project Memory\n   153→\n   154→### [openclaude-improved](https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/openclaude-improved)\n   155→runs anywhere. uses anything. A versatile Claude-based agent with broad model support.\n   156→- **Launch Date:** July 26, 2026\n   157→- **Category:** Multi-Model Agent\n   158→\n   159→### [pinvou-agent](https://github.com/Pinvou/pinvou-agent)\n   160→Open-source desktop AI agent for tools, files, knowledge, workflows, and real deliverables.\n   161→- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n   162→- **Category:** Desktop Agent/Knowledge Management\n   163→\n   164→### [goutoujunshi](https://github.com/powerycy/goutoujunshi)\n   165→一个先接住情绪、再分析关系并给出可执行策略的 Codex 恋爱军师，内置心理、法律、社会、人文、哲学、婚姻家庭与性学知识库。A Codex relationship advisor that first addresses emotions, then analyzes relationships and provides actionable strategies.\n   166→- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n   167→- **Category:** Specialized Agent/Domain Knowledge\n   168→\n   169→---\n   170→\n   171→## 5. Open-Source AI Coding Agents\n   172→\n   173→### [Cindy](https://github.com/makecindy/cindy)\n   174→Consider it done. The open-source AI agent that works out of the box. 想到，就能做到。开源、开箱即用的 AI Agent。\n   175→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   176→- **Category:** Open-Source Agent\n   177→- **Homepage:** https://cindy.app\n   178→\n   179→### [KlaatCode](https://github.com/KlaatAI/klaatcode)\n   180→Open-source AI coding agent for the terminal. Claude Code-grade accuracy with smart model routing.\n   181→- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n   182→- **Category:** Open-Source CLI Agent\n   183→\n   184→### [BossConsole](https://github.com/risa-labs-inc/BossConsole)\n   185→Open-source, multi-platform harness for AI agents.\n   186→- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n   187→- **Category:** Open-Source IDE Harness\n   188→\n   189→### [bbarit-agent-oss](https://github.com/bbarit/bbarit-agent-oss)\n   190→Open-source AI coding agent for your terminal — one Rust binary, 15+ LLM providers, 1,000+ models. A self-hostable Claude Code / Codex CLI alternative (MIT).\n   191→- **Launch Date:** July 16, 2026\n   192→- **Category:** Open-Source CLI Agent\n   193→\n   194→### [CoDes](https://github.com/sorsama/CoDes)\n   195→Open-source desktop workspace for running coding-agent CLIs side by side.\n   196→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   197→- **Category:** Open-Source Desktop Workspace\n   198→\n   199→### [approving](https://github.com/cocofhu/approving)\n   200→Approving is an open-source, self-hostable platform for turning coding agents into visual, reviewable, and recoverable delivery workflows. Agents run in real Docker sandboxes, exchange structured artifacts, and pause for human Approve at critical nodes.\n   201→- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n   202→- **Category:** Open-Source Workflow Platform\n   203→\n   204→### [autodev-studio](https://github.com/krishagarwal314/autodev-studio)\n   205→Autonomous multi-agent SDLC harness: describe a feature in plain English and AI agents scope, code, test, review, and open a PR — grounded in a one-time knowledge base of your repo.\n   206→- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n   207→- **Category:** Open-Source SDLC Platform\n   208→\n   209→### [DarkPs-Agent-CLI](https://github.com/dark-ps/DarkPs-Agent-CLI)\n   210→Extensible local-first AI agent framework for automation, coding, tools, and multi-model workflows.\n   211→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   212→- **Category:** Open-Source Agent Framework\n   213→\n   214→### [argus](https://github.com/Elysium-Labs-EU/argus)\n   215→Deterministic supervisor for multi-agent AI coding workflows: spawns workers, verifies diffs against git (not self-reports), and ships PRs. Written in Go.\n   216→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   217→- **Category:** Open-Source Workflow Supervisor\n   218→\n   219→### [AutoAgent-VersionCode](https://github.com/jaydenqiu51/AutoAgent-VersionCode)\n   220→An AI Coding Agent Framework lets multiple AI agents work together on software projects. Specialized agents plan, write code, test, debug, review, and document code while sharing project context.\n   221→- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n   222→- **Category:** Open-Source Multi-Agent Framework\n   223→\n   224→---\n   225→\n   226→## 6. IDE-Integrated AI Tools\n   227→\n   228→### [cv4vs-agents](https://github.com/Corsinvest/cv4vs-agents)\n   229→Agentic coding inside Visual Studio — Claude Code with a rich chat pane, an interactive terminal, and the IDE (editor, solution, debugger) exposed to the agent over MCP.\n   230→- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n   231→- **Category:** Visual Studio Integration\n   232→\n   233→### [nvim-agent-workbench](https://github.com/shanxierdan/nvim-agent-workbench)\n   234→A project-aware Neovim IDE with persistent Codex sessions, tmux resume, and one-command setup.\n   235→- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n   236→- **Category:** Neovim Integration\n   237→\n   238→### [Godot MCP Bridge](https://github.com/TomasLucasUTN/godot-mcp-bridge)\n   239→MCP server for Godot 4 — give Claude, Cursor, or any MCP client full control of the Godot editor: 228 tools, live-tree editing with undo, DAP step debugger, GDScript LSP, runtime play-testing.\n   240→- **Launch Date:** July 25, 2026\n   241→- **Category:** Game Engine IDE Integration\n   242→\n   243→### [Agents Council](https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/agents-council)\n   244→Multi-agents collaboration plugin for Claude Code - orchestrate multiple AI agents (Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, etc.) for diverse perspectives.\n   245→- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n   246→- **Category:** Multi-Agent Orchestration Plugin\n   247→\n   248→---\n   249→\n   250→## 7. Workflow Orchestration Agents\n   251→\n   252→### [shipmates](https://github.com/saman-mb/shipmates)\n   253→A crew of Claude Code sub-agents and slash-command workflows that drive a GitHub issue from open to a reviewed, CI-green pull request — autonomously. Flagship: /ship-issue.\n   254→- **Launch Date:** July 24, 2026\n   255→- **Category:** GitHub Workflow Automation\n   256→\n   257→### [ECC](https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC)\n   258→The agent harness performance optimization system for Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor.\n   259→- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n   260→- **Category:** Performance Optimization\n   261→\n   262→### [agentic-awesome-skills](https://github.com/sickn33/agentic-awesome-skills)\n   263→Local, agent-first control plane with 1,987+ agentic skills, including CLI and MCP integration.\n   264→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   265→- **Category:** Skills Platform/Control Plane\n   266→\n   267→### [agentic-awesome-kits](https://github.com/KhaiTrang1995/agentic-awesome-kits)\n   268→A universal collection of reusable Loop Engineering kits for AI coding agents—not just prompts. Each kit combines Skills, Rules, Templates, workflows, and validation loops.\n   269→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n   270→- **Category:** Workflow Templates/Kits\n   271→\n   272→### [agent-plugin-core](https://github.com/cs68614-hash/agent-plugin-core)\n   273→Codex plugin foundation for native MCP App widgets, semantic tools, versioned state, automation skills, and verified agent workflows.\n   274→- **Launch Date:** July 15, 2026\n   275→- **Category:** Plugin Foundation/Architecture\n   276→\n   277→### [kyn-agent-studio](https://github.com/cakbudak/kyn-agent-studio)\n   278→Build typed agent workflows and operate every run from authoritative evidence — OpenAI Build Week 2026.\n   279→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   280→- **Category:** Workflow Studio\n   281→\n   282→### [real-agent-workflows](https://github.com/qianquandong/real-agent-workflows)\n   283→The AI workflows I actually run, open-sourced one at a time. Each one is a plain-markdown playbook — trigger, steps, output — not a plugin, and not locked to any tool.\n   284→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   285→- **Category:** Workflow Playbooks\n   286→\n   287→### [symphlo](https://github.com/huisezhiyin/symphlo)\n   288→Local-first runtime for observable, debuggable AI-agent workflows with slidable autonomy and multi-agent/tool orchestration.\n   289→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   290→- **Category:** Workflow Runtime/Orchestration\n   291→\n   292→---\n   293→\n   294→## Additional Notable Tools\n   295→\n   296→### [hwatu](https://github.com/hongnoul/hwatu)\n   297→Fast, interruptible verification browser for AI coding agents: 35 ms checks, pixel diffs, live human hand-off.\n   298→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   299→- **Category:** Verification/Testing\n   300→\n   301→### [cyvisguard](https://github.com/flankerhqd/cyvisguard)\n   302→Security control plane for AI agents — identity and delegation, capability policy, data-flow taint and a live audit trail, enforced over MCP.\n   303→- **Launch Date:** July 22, 2026\n   304→- **Category:** Security/Governance\n   305→\n   306→### [sigbound](https://github.com/surya-koritala/sigbound)\n   307→Run AI coding agents in parallel on one git repo and safely auto-merge their work — only changes that build and pass tests land.\n   308→- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n   309→- **Category:** CI/CD Integration\n   310→\n   311→### [mentor](https://github.com/smixs/mentor)\n   312→A session-insights skill for AI coding agents. Reads your local Claude Code and OpenAI Codex history and writes an /insights-style HTML report on how you work.\n   313→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   314→- **Category:** Analytics/Insights\n   315→\n   316→### [pm-manager](https://github.com/wei63w/pm-manager)\n   317→Know what to fix next — local .pm governance skill pack for AI coding agents.\n   318→- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n   319→- **Category:** Project Management\n   320→\n   321→### [rtk](https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk)\n   322→CLI proxy that reduces LLM token consumption by 60-90% on common dev commands.\n   323→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   324→- **Category:** Token Optimization\n   325→\n   326→### [codeburn](https://github.com/getagentseal/codeburn)\n   327→Local tool tracking token usage and cost across 31 AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini.\n   328→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   329→- **Category:** Cost Tracking\n   330→\n   331→### [awesome-ai-tokenomics](https://github.com/QuesmaOrg/awesome-ai-tokenomics)\n   332→A map of what AI tokens actually cost, and where they're wasted vs. well spent.\n   333→- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n   334→- **Category:** Cost Optimization/Research\n   335→\n   336→### [ruvnet/ruflo](https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo)\n   337→Multi-agent harness for deploying swarms, coordinating workflows, with adaptive memory and RAG integration.\n   338→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   339→- **Category:** Swarm Orchestration\n   340→\n   341→### [oraios/serena](https://github.com/oraios/serena)\n   342→MCP toolkit providing semantic retrieval and editing capabilities, described as \"the IDE for your agent\".\n   343→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   344→- **Category:** Agent IDE/Toolkit\n   345→\n   346→### [agno](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno)\n   347→Platform to \"build, run, and manage agent platforms\".\n   348→- **Launch Date:** July 29, 2026\n   349→- **Category:** Agent Platform\n   350→\n   351→### [tirth8205/code-review-graph](https://github.com/tirth8205/code-review-graph)\n   352→Local-first code intelligence graph for MCP and CLI building persistent maps of codebases.\n   353→- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n   354→- **Category:** Code Analysis/Graph\n   355→\n   356→### [yvgude/lean-ctx](https://github.com/yvgude/lean-ctx)\n   357→Context intelligence layer deciding \"what they read, remembers what they learn\" with 60-90% fewer tokens.\n   358→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   359→- **Category:** Context Optimization\n   360→\n   361→### [metalbear-co/mirrord](https://github.com/metalbear-co/mirrord)\n   362→Runs processes on local machines or AI agent environments as if in Kubernetes pods.\n   363→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   364→- **Category:** DevOps/Cloud Integration\n   365→\n   366→---\n   367→\n   368→## MCP Server Ecosystem (July 15-29, 2026)\n   369→\n   370→### [livetennisapi-mcp](https://github.com/livetennisapi/livetennisapi-mcp)\n   371→MCP server for the Live Tennis API — give Claude, Cursor and other LLM agents real-time tennis scores, odds and model win-probability.\n   372→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   373→\n   374→### [Stormy Social Data API](https://github.com/OneInterface/stormy-cookbook)\n   375→Open-source cookbook for the Stormy Social Data API and MCP server — one REST API for TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, LinkedIn, X (Twitter), and Reddit.\n   376→- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n   377→\n   378→### [App Store Connect MCP](https://github.com/erayendes/app-store-connect-mcp)\n   379→Heimdall — MCP server for the Apple App Store Connect API & App Store Server API (StoreKit 2). 982 tools from Apple's official OpenAPI spec.\n   380→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   381→\n   382→### [Godot MCP Go](https://github.com/regiellis/godot-mcp-go)\n   383→Control a running Godot 4.7 editor and game directly from the terminal. Includes a Go CLI, editor addon, 312 commands, and an MCP server.\n   384→- **Launch Date:** July 23, 2026\n   385→\n   386→### [symbolpeek-mcp](https://github.com/pioner92/symbolpeek-mcp)\n   387→Token-efficient MCP server giving AI coding agents symbol-level reads of TS/JS, Rust, Python, Java, Go, JSON, and Markdown.\n   388→- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n   389→\n   390→### [mcpgrade](https://github.com/TengByte/mcpgrade)\n   391→Lighthouse for MCP servers — score any MCP server on agent usability, not just spec compliance.\n   392→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   393→\n   394→---\n   395→\n   396→## Summary Statistics\n   397→\n   398→- **Total Tools Discovered:** 80+ AI coding tools\n   399→- **Open-Source Projects:** ~90%\n   400→- **Most Active Launch Dates:** July 15, 17, 18, 20-22, 24, 28-29\n   401→- **Primary Categories:**\n   402→  1. CLI/Terminal Agents (15+ tools)\n   403→  2. Open-Source Agent Frameworks (12+ tools)\n   404→  3. Workflow Orchestration (10+ tools)\n   405→  4. IDE Integrations (8+ tools)\n   406→  5. Memory/Context Tools (6+ tools)\n   407→  6. Security/Governance (5+ tools)\n   408→  7. MCP Servers (15+ tools)\n   409→\n   410→## Key Trends\n   411→\n   412→1. **Terminal-based AI agents** are exploding as a category\n   413→2. **Multi-agent orchestration** is becoming mainstream\n   414→3. **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** ecosystem is rapidly expanding\n   415→4. **Cost optimization** tools (token tracking, smart routing) are emerging\n   416→5. **Memory persistence** across agent sessions is a major focus\n   417→6. **Security and governance** tooling is maturing\n   418→7. **Workflow standardization** through templates and playbooks\n   419→\n   420→---\n   421→\n   422→**Research Date:** July 29, 2026\n   423→**Time Period:** July 15-29, 2026 (14 days)\n   424→**Sources:** GitHub API, GitHub Trending, Product Hunt, Hacker News, DEV Community, Lobsters\n   425→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
